  "verbalization": "Angoroside-C is implicated in the interaction with Caspase-5, which is a key target for multiple compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid, all of which have a shared target of NH-6. This suggests a potential pathway where Angoroside-C may act through Caspase-5 to influence NH-6, possibly via a common mechanism involving proteolytic activity or signaling pathways. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Angoroside-C is linked to a series of compounds that ultimately target NH-6, suggesting a possible role in modulating cellular processes through Caspase-5. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Angoroside-C may exert its effects through Caspase-5, which in turn affects NH-6, potentially through a shared biological mechanism. The evidence supports a mechanism where Angoroside-C could be part of a broader network of compounds that interact with Caspase-5 and ultimately influence NH-6.",
